# CODEOWNERS — GitHub code-owner review enforcement (SAAS-INFRA).
#
# Per GitHub docs: each line is `<path-pattern> <owner1> <owner2> ...`. The
# LAST matching pattern wins (same semantics as .gitignore). Owners must be
# GitHub team handles prefixed with `@` (we use the `@outrena/<team>` org
# scope — replace with real team slugs if your org differs).
#
# Real team mapping (documented in runbooks/00-README.md):
#   @outrena/platform-team  — overall infra + CI + cross-cutting concerns
#   @outrena/backend-team   — Python backend (app/, tests/)
#   @outrena/frontend-team  — TypeScript frontend (src/)
#   @outrena/devops-team    — Terraform + GitHub workflows + Helm chart
#   @outrena/security-team  — SOC2 + secrets + security.yml
#   @outrena/sre-team       — runbooks + on-call + monitoring
#
# Branch protection (configured in GitHub repo settings — see runbook 10):
#   - main + develop require CODEOWNERS review on PR.
#   - The `/.github/` paths require BOTH @security-team + @devops-team approval.

# ── Default owner (fallback for anything not matched below) ──────────────────
*                                         @outrena/platform-team

# ── Backend (Python) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/outrena-backend/                        @outrena/backend-team
/outrena-backend/app/                    @outrena/backend-team
/outrena-backend/tests/                  @outrena/backend-team
/outrena-backend/alembic/                @outrena/backend-team
/outrena-backend/pyproject.toml          @outrena/backend-team
/outrena-backend/.env.example            @outrena/backend-team @outrena/security-team

